 - 2026-06-11: GOAL-INDUCTION SEPARATION (the planning-layer prerequisite Deep Think Q2 named): on an ARC-AGI-3 game where we ALREADY have a verifier-certified world model (r11l L1-L3, or vc33 at 99% dynamics accuracy), induce the GOAL PREDICATE -- the function over a state that returns solved/not-solved -- SEPARATELY from the dynamics rule, from the OBSERVED level-up transitions (the frame just before a level_completed signal). The dynamics model (T(s,a)->s') and the goal predicate (is_goal(s)) are DIFFERENT objects; this milestone treats them separately because a verifier gives validity, not direction -- the goal predicate is half of the missing navigator. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: goal_predicate_induced_heldout_precision_1.000; results/experiment_4020_goal_induction_separation.json
 - 2026-06-11: HEURISTIC SEARCH OVER THE VERIFIED WORLD MODEL (THE CENTRAL BET of the Deep-Think pivot): implement a planning search -- bounded best-first / A* / depth-limited MCTS -- over the induced+verifier-certified world model from exp4020, with the VERIFIER as the forward simulator (legal next-state expansion + the exp4020 goal test) and a heuristic value (distance-to-goal proxy: cells-to-goal, progress-bar delta, object-alignment, or a learned/coded heuristic) providing the directional gradient the verifier cannot. TARGET: break a planning wall that single-step re-induce->validate->act STALLED on (r11l L4, or vc33 -- where a 99%-accurate verified WM still failed to solve). This is the direct test of Deep Think Q2 (dynamics != heuristics: does adding a SEPARATE navigator over the verified simulator advance past the wall?) AND of the modality-mismatch steelman (if search over the code-represented WM SOLVES it, the wall was SEARCH not representation -- which our vc33 99%-WM data predicts). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: search_layer_solved_r11l_L4_real_env_confirmed; results/experiment_4021_heuristic_search_over_verified_wm.json
 - 2026-06-11: DECENTRALIZATION next step, DATA-GATED on exp4012's actual best-of-N result (Deep Think confidently claimed best-of-N is hopeless; exp4012 measured it -- read the number, then branch). IF exp4012 showed local best-of-N (k=8-16, gemma-4-12B) BEAT vote / materially lifted induction: run a SCALING confirmation (higher k, or a second local model) -- the sovereign path is viable. IF it did NOT (Deep Think's structural-representational-deficit right -- best-of-N yields confident failures): prototype the VERIFIER-AS-REWARD distillation FEASIBILITY (the alternative sovereignty path): collect N verifier-certified (demo-perfect, execution-validated) induction traces from the codex+verifier stack as a fine-tune corpus, and measure the feasibility (corpus size achievable, trace quality, a SMALL fine-tune sanity check on a tiny subset) -- a FEASIBILITY scoping, NOT a full multi-hour distillation train. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: B_distill_feasibility_exp4012_no_lift_clean_traces40_sanity_delta1.097; results/experiment_4022_decentralization_gated.json
